---
// Startseite — Umbau nach E-C321 und E-C319 (FXR-2011, 2026-11-19).
//
// Die Seite beginnt mit dem PROBLEM des Kunden, nicht mit einer Funktion (E-C321:
// „FALSCH, WENN die Startseite nach dem Umbau mit einer Funktion statt mit dem Problem des
// Kunden beginnt oder eine Stufe eine Funktion vorenthaelt").
//
// Abschnittsfolge:
//   1 Hero: der Nachmittag  ·  2 Vier Wege, auf denen eine Bewertung endet  ·  3 Die Zahl (R)
//   4 Der erste Trade in fuenfzehn Minuten  ·  5 Ein Weg vom ersten Backtest bis zum echten
//   Konto (Leiter Defined · Rehearsed · Proven · Live, dazu Backtest und Journal)
//   6 Mehrere Konten, mehrere Firmen  ·  7 Was FixedR nicht tut, drei Zusagen
//   8 Preis (jede Stufe hat alles)  ·  9 Founders und Warteliste
//
// ⚠️ KANVAS (FXR-239): die Vorgaengerfassung war aus `temp/export-web-v6` uebertragen. Dieser
// Umbau ist im Kanvas NICHT nachgezogen — der naechste Export liefe gegen diesen Bestand.
// Die Buehne (Abschnitt 6), der Hero-Aufbau, Backtest/Journal-Bilder und die dunkle
// Schlussflaeche sind unveraendert uebernommen; neu sind `.wege`, `.erster`, `.weg` und der
// Preisblock. Entfallen: die vier Sprungkacheln und „Eleven parts" (steht auf /product).
//
// Regeln fuer jeden Text hier: keine Geldbetraege von Trades (nur R und Prozent), kein
// Garantieversprechen, keine Wettbewerbernamen, nichts, was der Code nicht hat.
import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';
import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ReifegradChip from '../components/ReifegradChip.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';

// FXR-164: der Produktfilm existiert noch nicht. Ohne Datei bleibt es beim Standbild,
// ohne Konsolenfehler — die Einbindung ist vorbereitet (stumm, Schleife, Poster).
const heroVideoExists = existsSync(
  fileURLToPath(new URL('../../public/videos/product-loop.mp4', import.meta.url)),
);
const SCREEN = '/20261109_Lander_Screen.png';

// Abschnitt 2 — je Karte: die Lage, was FixedR an dieser Stelle tut, was dadurch wegfaellt.
// Der Reifegrad kommt aus `content/reifegrad.ts`; eine id ohne Eintrag bricht den Bau.
const wege = [
  {
    nr: '01', titel: 'The stop got moved',
    lage: 'Just this once, to give the trade room. Or there was no stop at all.',
    tut: 'No stop, no trade. The risk is fixed before entry, not renegotiated while the position runs.',
    ergebnis: 'What a trade may lose is decided before it exists.',
    reife: 'mandatory-stop',
  },
  {
    nr: '02', titel: 'The size was wrong',
    lage: 'Lots worked out in your head while the candle runs.',
    tut: 'You choose the risk. FixedR computes the size from your stop distance.',
    ergebnis: 'Every trade carries the risk you chose, with no arithmetic under time pressure.',
    reife: 'position-size-from-risk',
  },
  {
    nr: '03', titel: 'The limit was hit',
    lage: 'Daily loss or drawdown, crossed in the run of trades after the first loss.',
    tut: "Your firm's rule set belongs to the account and is checked before the order leaves.",
    ergebnis: 'The account does not fall to a rule you already knew. A net, not a guarantor.',
    reife: 'firm-rule-profiles',
  },
  {
    nr: '04', titel: 'The trade ran into the news',
    lage: 'A release you knew about, at a moment you were not watching.',
    tut: 'A news window with a buffer locks the affected symbol. The times come from the economic calendar.',
    ergebnis: 'Reacting in time no longer depends on you sitting at the screen.',
    reife: 'news-protection',
  },
];

// Abschnitt 4 — das Sofort-Erlebnis, wortnah an /product/start.
const ersteSchritte = [
  { nr: '01', titel: 'Connect a demo account', text: 'MetaTrader 5 or NinjaTrader 8, with a guide that points at the real control on the real screen.' },
  { nr: '02', titel: 'Click an entry and a stop', text: 'On the chart. Without a stop, the order does not exist.' },
  { nr: '03', titel: 'Choose the risk', text: 'A fraction of a unit of risk, not a lot size.' },
  { nr: '04', titel: 'The size is there', text: 'Computed on the spot. The trade runs in R, with the distance to your daily limit right next to it.' },
];

// Abschnitt 5 — die Leiter (E-C321). Im Code: DRAFT · BACKTEST_VALIDATED · TEST_PROVEN · LIVE
// (awesome-cockpit `trading-cockpit/src/lib/strategyJourney.ts`). Oben steht „Live", nie
// „funded" oder „profitable". Die Leiter fuehrt nur, sie sperrt nichts.
const leiter = [
  { stufe: 'Defined', wo: 'On paper', text: 'The strategy is written down once: its steps, its rules, as a version.' },
  { stufe: 'Rehearsed', wo: 'Backtest', text: 'Traded on past markets in replay, with the future hidden.' },
  { stufe: 'Proven', wo: 'Test', text: 'Traded on the running market in the test environment, with nothing at stake.' },
  { stufe: 'Live', wo: 'Your accounts', text: 'Traded on your accounts, under the rules of each firm.' },
];
const verbindung = [
  'The journal fills itself, because the order was set here first.',
  'The same order ticket in backtest, test and live. What you practise is what you do.',
  'One strategy, one record: you see what state it is in, and every change of the rules starts the evidence again.',
];

// Abschnitt 7 — drei Zusagen (FXR-1765). Aussagen ueber die Bedingungen, nie ueber den Trader.
const zusagen = [
  { nr: '01', titel: 'No money on screen', text: 'Risk, result and distance to the limit appear only in R and percent. There is no toggle that brings a currency view back.', link: null },
  { nr: '02', titel: 'Your trading data stays on your machine', text: 'FixedR runs locally on Windows. Your trades, accounts and journal never reach us. You sign in with a FixedR account for the licence.', link: { href: '/trust', text: 'What does cross the line is on Trust →' } },
  { nr: '03', titel: 'You place every trade', text: 'No bot, no signals, no black box. FixedR enforces your own rules and records what happened; the decision stays with the trader.', link: null },
];

const buehneTitel = ['One ticket · three accounts', 'Linked symbols', 'Payout protection', 'Your month in R'];

const verteilung = [
  { konto: 'FTMO 100k', wert: '4.2', ok: true },
  { konto: 'Apex 150k', wert: '6.1', ok: true },
  { konto: 'Lucid 50k', wert: 'not configured', ok: false },
];
// Verknuepfte Symbole: derselbe Markt heisst je Konto anders (awesome-cockpit
// `AssetMappingService`, FXR-1907/FXR-1908: EURUSD-Trade ueber das verknuepfte Instrument 6E).
const verknuepft = [
  { konto: 'FTMO 100k · MetaTrader', symbol: 'EURUSD' },
  { konto: 'Apex 150k · NinjaTrader', symbol: '6E' },
];

const werte = [0, 1.2, -0.4, 2.1, 0, 0, 0, 0.8, 1.9, -1, 0.5, 3.2, 0, 0, -0.6, 2.4, 1.1, 0, 0.9, 1.4, 0, 0, -0.3, 1.8, 2.6, 0.7, -1.2, 0];
const monatDunkel = werte.map((w) => {
  const leer = w === 0;
  const stark = w >= 1.8;
  return {
    wert: leer ? '' : (w > 0 ? '+' : '−') + Math.abs(w).toFixed(1),
    stil: `display:grid;place-items:center;height:38px;border-radius:8px;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;background:${leer ? 'var(--ink-3)' : w > 0 ? (stark ? 'var(--brand-on-ink)' : 'rgba(46,134,246,.22)') : 'var(--ink-3)'};border:1px solid ${leer ? 'var(--ink-line)' : 'transparent'};color:${w > 0 ? (stark ? '#fff' : 'var(--brand-on-ink)') : 'var(--on-ink-muted)'}`,
  };
});

// Kerzen der Replay-Karte: deterministisch aus dem Index, damit jeder Bau gleich aussieht
// und ein Bildvergleich ueberhaupt etwas wert ist.
const kerzen = Array.from({ length: 26 }, (_, i) => {
  const y = 26 + Math.sin(i * 0.55) * 12 + i * 0.9 + (i % 3) * 4;
  const hh = 10 + ((i * 7) % 18);
  const auf = (i * 7) % 5 < 3;
  const c = auf ? 'var(--on-ink-muted)' : 'var(--ink-line-2)';
  return `position:absolute;left:${4 + i * 3.6}%;top:${y}%;width:1.9%;height:${hh}%;border-radius:1px;background:${c};box-shadow:0 -${hh * 0.25}px 0 0 ${c},0 ${hh * 0.2}px 0 0 ${c};opacity:${auf ? 0.85 : 1}`;
});

const plan = [['Setup', 'Pullback'], ['Entry', '17,830'], ['Stop', '17,812 · 1.0 R'], ['Target', '17,866 · 2.0 R']].map(([k, v]) => ({ k, v }));
const ergebnis = [
  ['Closed', '17,861', 'color:var(--on-ink)'],
  ['Result', '+1.7 R', 'color:var(--brand-on-ink);font-weight:600'],
  ['Stop moved', 'no', 'color:var(--on-ink)'],
  ['Rule check', 'held', 'color:var(--on-ink)'],
].map(([k, v, stil]) => ({ k, v, stil }));

// ── Preisblock nach E-C319 / E-C321 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Jede Stufe hat ALLE Funktionen; unterschieden wird nur die Zahl der gleichzeitig
// handelbaren Konten und das, was daraus zwingend folgt (Verteilen auf mehrere Konten).
// Basispreis nach E-C321, hoehere Stufen und Schwellen sind NICHT entschieden: sie stehen
// als „to be announced" da, nicht als erfundene Zahl. Kein Preisanker mit Summe („ueber
// 100") — nicht nachgemessen; genannt werden nur die Gattungen ohne Preis.
// Stufennamen nach Kontenzahl, nicht „Basic" (klingt abgespeckt).
const ersetzt = ['a charting subscription', 'a journal subscription', 'a replay subscription'];
const inJederStufe = [
  'Mandatory stop, position size from your risk',
  "Your firm's rule set, checked before the order leaves",
  'News window and payout protection',
  'Everything in R and percent, no money view',
  'A journal that fills itself, metrics in R',
  'Backtest with replay, and test trading',
  'Strategies with versions, from Defined to Live',
  'Charts, indicators and layouts, none capped by plan',
];
const stufen = [
  {
    name: 'One account', preis: '€29', einheit: '/ month', offen: false,
    satz: 'One account tradable at a time.',
    konten: ['1 account at a time'],
  },
  {
    name: 'A few accounts', preis: 'To be announced', einheit: '', offen: true,
    satz: 'Several accounts at once, at one firm or at several.',
    konten: ['A few accounts at a time (number to be announced)', 'One order, distributed across your accounts'],
  },
  {
    name: 'Many accounts', preis: 'To be announced', einheit: '', offen: true,
    satz: 'For running many accounts in parallel.',
    konten: ['Many or unlimited accounts (to be decided)', 'One order, distributed across your accounts'],
  },
];

// Abschnitt 9 — was man mit der Anmeldung bekommt.
const bekommst = [
  { t: 'The guide, right after signup', d: 'Eight short chapters on the problems that end a challenge more often than the strategy does, and what closes each one.' },
  { t: 'A seat in the founders circle', d: 'A small group first, then the waitlist, in order of signup.' },
  { t: 'The founders price', d: 'Reduced for a limited time, and stated in your invitation.' },
  { t: 'A say in what comes next', d: 'The first traders shape what gets built.' },
];
---
<Base bare>
  <!-- ═══ 1 · Hero: der Nachmittag ═══ -->
  <section class="home-hero">
    <span class="raster" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="big-r-wrap" aria-hidden="true"><span class="big-r">R</span></span>
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">The trading environment for prop traders — practise, test and trade in one place</p>
        <h1>Most evaluations don't die from a bad strategy. <span class="accent">They die in one bad afternoon.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">
          FixedR is built for that afternoon: no trade without a stop, size computed from your
          risk, your firm's limits checked before the order leaves — and
          <strong>no balance on the screen to negotiate with.</strong> Trade, journal and
          backtest in one place, in R.
        </p>
        <span class="actions">
          <a class="btn" href="/waitlist">Join the waitlist</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="#four-ways">Four ways an evaluation ends</a>
        </span>
        <p class="meta">
          <span class="lbl">WORKS WITH</span>
          <span class="chip">MetaTrader</span>
          <span class="chip">NinjaTrader</span>
          <span class="rest">· runs on your machine · trading data stays local</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      {/* Michael 2026-09-11: die Karte nimmt ihre Höhe vom Bild, damit jeder Screenshot
          vollständig und randlos sitzt — kein festes Verhältnis, kein `scale` auf dem
          Inhalt. Das bewacht `tools/guards.mjs`. */}
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="stage-content">
          {heroVideoExists ? (
            <video class="stage-video" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster={SCREEN} aria-hidden="true">
              <source src="/videos/product-loop.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
            </video>
          ) : (
            <img src={SCREEN} alt="The FixedR cockpit: two synchronised M15 charts with sessions and pivot levels, dark mode" width="2880" height="1662" />
          )}
        </div>
        <div class="stage-veil">
          <span class="play-btn" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"></path></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="stage-caption">
            <span class="stage-title">One trade, in R, start to finish.</span>
            {heroVideoExists && <span class="stage-sub">45 s · no sound needed</span>}
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ 2 · Vier Wege, auf denen eine Bewertung endet ═══ -->
  <section class="wege" id="four-ways">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="kopf" data-reveal>
        <span class="eyebrow">Where the afternoon goes wrong</span>
        <h2>Four ways an evaluation ends.</h2>
        <p>None of them is the strategy. Each one is a moment where the platform could have held a rule and left it to you instead.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="karten" data-reveal>
        {wege.map((w) => (
          <div class="karte">
            <span class="nr"><span>{w.nr}</span><span class="ln"></span><ReifegradChip id={w.reife} /></span>
            <span class="t">{w.titel}</span>
            <span class="lage">{w.lage}</span>
            <span class="zeile"><span class="lbl">What FixedR does</span><span class="d">{w.tut}</span></span>
            <span class="zeile"><span class="lbl">What that ends</span><span class="d">{w.ergebnis}</span></span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ 3 · Die Zahl: R statt Geld ═══ -->
  <section class="akt1" id="the-number">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="lead" data-reveal>
        <span class="eyebrow">The number</span>
        <h2>Loud charts. Calm numbers. Trade in R.</h2>
        <p>
          There is a fifth way, and it sits behind the other four: the money number. It changes
          scale with every account and pulls at you on every trade. R does neither. So we did
          not add a warning. We changed the scale.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/manifesto">Read the manifesto →</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="regeln">
        <div class="regel" data-reveal>
          <span class="kreis">01</span>
          <span class="txt">
            <span class="t">Money stays out of sight</span>
            <span class="d">Results, targets, drawdown headroom — all in R and percent. No money mode, no toggle. The absence is the feature.</span>
            {/* Der unscharfe Fleck neben dem scharfen R-Wert ist das Argument. Er traegt
                bewusst KEINE Zahl mehr (FXR-2011: keine Geldbetraege von Trades, auch nicht
                unlesbar im Quelltext) — vorher stand hier ein verwischter Betrag. */}
            <span class="bild" style="align-items:baseline;gap:12px">
              <span style="font-size:22px;font-weight:600">+2.4 R</span>
              <span class="verwischt" aria-hidden="true">■■■■■■</span>
            </span>
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="regel" data-reveal>
          <span class="kreis">02</span>
          <span class="txt">
            <span class="t">One unit, from the first evaluation to the largest account</span>
            <span class="d">R is defined by your own risk. The screen reads the same on a 10k account and on a 100k account, so the routine does not change when the account does.</span>
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="regel" data-reveal>
          <span class="kreis">03</span>
          <span class="txt">
            <span class="t">There's no money in this account. Only a number and a scale.</span>
            <span class="d">
              The balance of a funded account is notional — it isn't your money, and often not
              literal capital at all. What's real is your distance to the drawdown limit and to
              the target, both defined in percent. A currency display suggests a concreteness
              that doesn't exist. So we removed it.
            </span>
          </span>
        </div>
        <span class="schluss-linie"></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ 4 · Der erste Trade in fuenfzehn Minuten ═══ -->
  <section class="erster" id="first-trade">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="kopf" data-reveal>
        <span class="eyebrow">The first fifteen minutes</span>
        <h2>Your first trade in R, inside fifteen minutes.</h2>
        <p>
          You do not put in weeks before you find out what this does. Connect a demo account
          and place one trade: that sequence is the whole idea, experienced instead of described.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="schritte" data-reveal>
        {ersteSchritte.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <span class="nr">{s.nr}</span>
            <span class="t">{s.titel}</span>
            <span class="d">{s.text}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p class="fuss" data-reveal>
        Fifteen minutes teach the mechanics, not the strategy. <a href="/product/start">How the start works →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ 5 · Ein Weg vom ersten Backtest bis zum echten Konto ═══ -->
  <section class="weg" id="one-path">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="kopf" data-reveal>
        <span class="eyebrow">One environment</span>
        <h2>One path from your first backtest to the live account.</h2>
        <p>
          Practised in one tool, traded in another, reviewed in a third: none of them knew
          your rules. Here a strategy is one object that moves through four states, and the
          journal and the metrics run through all of them.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="leiter" data-reveal>
        {leiter.map((l, i) => (
          <div class="stufe">
            <span class="nr">{`0${i + 1}`}</span>
            <span class="t">{l.stufe}</span>
            <span class="wo">{l.wo}</span>
            <span class="d">{l.text}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <span class="band"><span class="lbl">Journal</span><span class="d">written by the trade itself, in every state</span></span>
        <span class="band"><span class="lbl">Metrics in R</span><span class="d">the same kind of record from the first backtest on</span></span>
      </div>
      <p class="hinweis" data-reveal>
        Where a strategy stands is counted from its own trades in each environment. You set
        the thresholds or switch them off. The ladder shows the way; it does not block a trade.
      </p>
      <ul class="saetze" data-reveal>
        {verbindung.map((v) => <li>{v}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="hinweis" data-reveal>
        The honest limit: fills in backtest and test are simulated. Same handling, same rules,
        same record — not the fill your broker gives you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Backtest und Journal: die zwei Bilder zum Weg -->
  <section class="akt34">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="spalte" data-reveal>
        <div class="bild">
          {kerzen.map((c) => <span style={c}></span>)}
          <span style="position:absolute;left:62%;top:0;bottom:44px;width:1px;background:var(--brand-on-ink);opacity:.8"></span>
          <span style="position:absolute;left:62%;right:0;top:0;bottom:44px;background:repeating-linear-gradient(135deg,transparent 0 6px,rgba(46,134,246,.07) 6px 7px)"></span>
          <span class="mono" style="position:absolute;left:calc(62% + 10px);top:14px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:4px;background:var(--brand-on-ink);color:#fff;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em">FUTURE HIDDEN</span>
          <span class="mono" style="position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;height:44px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:0 14px;border-top:1px solid var(--ink-line);background:var(--ink-2);font-size:11px;color:var(--on-ink-muted)">
            <span style="width:26px;height:26px;display:grid;place-items:center;border-radius:6px;background:var(--brand-on-ink);color:#fff;font-size:11px">▶</span>
            <span>×4</span>
            <span style="margin-left:auto;color:var(--brand-on-ink);font-weight:600">+3.1 R</span>
          </span>
        </div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Rehearsed · Backtest</span>
        <h2>Your first losing streak shouldn't be the one that counts.</h2>
        <p>
          A backtest is only worth something if the trade goes in the way a real one does. So in
          FixedR it does — same order ticket, same mandatory stop, same size computed from your
          risk, same result in R. Scrolling back and guessing measures memory, not method.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="spalte" data-reveal>
        <div class="bild mono" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;font-size:12px;color:var(--on-ink-muted)">
          <span style="padding:18px;border-right:1px solid var(--ink-line);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px">
            <span style="font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--on-ink-faint)">PLAN · AT ENTRY</span>
            {plan.map((z) => <span style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px"><span>{z.k}</span><span style="color:var(--on-ink)">{z.v}</span></span>)}
          </span>
          <span style="padding:18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px">
            <span style="font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--on-ink-faint)">OUTCOME · AT CLOSE</span>
            {ergebnis.map((z) => <span style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px"><span>{z.k}</span><span style={z.stil}>{z.v}</span></span>)}
          </span>
        </div>
        <span class="eyebrow">In every state · Journal</span>
        <h2>The journal fills itself, because the order was set here first.</h2>
        <p>
          A journal that requires typing gets filled for a week and then stops. One that fills
          itself is still there in month three. The plan was the order ticket; the outcome is the
          trade as it closed. No export, no import, no sync — for every order placed through FixedR.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="ueberleitung" data-reveal>
      And all of it is open from day one. <a href="#pricing">Every plan has everything →</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ 6 · Mehrere Konten, mehrere Firmen: vier Schritte, eine feste Bühne ═══ -->
  <section class="akt2" id="several-accounts">
    <div class="kopf">
      <div class="txt" data-reveal>
        <span class="eyebrow">Several accounts, several firms</span>
        <h2>One trade, every account, each under its own rules.</h2>
        <p class="firmen">
          Rule profiles are maintained today for Apex, FTMO, IQ Capital and Lucid. In
          preparation: FundedNext, The5ers, MyFundedFutures, Blue Guardian, Alpha Capital Group
          and Sure Leverage Funding. Platforms: MetaTrader 5 and NinjaTrader 8.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="schritte">
        <div class="schritt" data-schritt="0" data-aktiv>
